+“The older woman looked over and eyed the soldier working on the unconscious man. “Soldier, what is his condition,” she asked, and the voice held authority, the authority of someone who was used to being deferred to in situations like this. The soldier without missing a beat or looking up began to speak softly as he pulled out bandages and salves. “I need to stabilize him, he is in bad shape, I am guessing multiple broken bones, swelling of the brain and internet bleeding, but he is alive,” he said continuing to work. The woman crawled over to the man and began examining him. “Are you a doctor?” Corliss finally asked and the woman simply nodded. “I need to get him someplace safe and soon, I need a hospital where I can work,” she said, locking eyes with Corliss and she could see the pleading in those eyes. With a nod, she motioned out the other teams. “Get me a gurney, I need it asap, we are brining him back with us” she finished, and the soldiers hesitated. Corliss knew why, these were mages, the Empress had been using Mages to enforce her new order and Silvan’s were already touchy. She shot him an annoyed look and he simply nodded taking off into the woods with two others. Politics be damned she thought resolving that she would not leave people to die simply to make a politician’s life easer.
+
+She stood there watching the two work on the young man, her team spread out to cover the field as they continued to try and stabilize him. Finally, the soldier returned with two long branches and cloth strung between them. They gently laid it down next to the man and with the supervision of the Mage Doctor and the medic, they moved him and lifted him gently. The entire group dissolved into the treeline making their way back towards the city. Corliss followed the precession keeping behind the man being carried as the older woman joined her, walking in silence for a few moments before speaking. “I wanted to thank you for saving us” She began, and Corliss made a motion for her to stop. “Its what we do, but I don’t know how the reception of more lowlanders will be to the Silvan’s,” she said, and the woman simply nodded. “The Silvan’s have always been a bit xenophobic, but the order does have some dealings with them so I am hoping that goodwill can be implied upon, this once,” she said smiling weakly. Corliss looked at the woman she did not know anyone had dealings with the Silvan’s but apparently, they had kept in contact with the mages at least. She filed that away for later and continued to walk. “I am Master Patrice, and this is Initiate Dara, the man you carry is Marcus Gavin,” she said looking at Marcus as he laid unconscious in front of them.
+
+“I am Warden Corliss,” she said and Patrice nodded “We had heard the Wardens had traveled North abandoning the keep,” she said, it was not an accusation nor was there any heat in the statement, it was simply a statement so Corliss did not try to defend it. She instead focused on the woman’s introduction, she had not given the man on the gurney a title, but Corliss spied the clothes, he was dressed as a mage. “Is that man not a mage?” she asked pointing to Marcus. She was quiet as Patrice regarded him and finally turned her head to look at Corliss. “He is, but not of the order. His story is different, but understand he is special and there are those who hunt for him, our only choice was to come here,” she said Corliss nodding and looking back at the man they carried.
 
